# A control plane holds the Botanist key, grants, issued credentials, workspaces
# and history. Every one of them is ignored, at any depth — test fixtures and
# substrate checkouts carry their own.
**/.tendril/

# The repository's OWN control plane is the exception, and only for the genome
# beneath it. Genome seeds are repository content rather than control-plane
# state: they are concatenated into every Sprout's system prompt, so they belong
# to the repository the Sprout works on.
#
# It takes three lines because git cannot re-include anything beneath an excluded
# DIRECTORY. So the directory is un-excluded, its contents are excluded instead,
# and the genome is re-included through that gap. Without this a new seed is
# silently untracked; the seeds that predate the rule survive only because they
# were already tracked when it landed.
!/.tendril/
/.tendril/*
!/.tendril/genome/

# Fitness is measured state, not authored content, so it stays out.
/.tendril/genome/fitness.json

# Private keys / secrets (e.g. GitHub App .pem) — never commit
*.pem
*.private-key.pem
*.swp
